WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:17.224
It was the final round of King Henry's archery contest.

2
00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:20.845
The Bishop of Hereford sat next to the queen.

3
00:00:21.505 --> 00:00:24.266
The king's page led three men onto the field.

4
00:00:24.746 --> 00:00:27.487
They were named Gilbert, Tepus, and Hubert.

5
00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:29.828
They bowed to the king and queen.

6
00:00:31.904 --> 00:00:34.727
The queen's page led three men onto the field.

7
00:00:35.447 --> 00:00:39.170
They were Robin Hood, Little John, and Will Scarlet.

8
00:00:39.811 --> 00:00:47.177
When the queen's archers bowed, the Bishop of Hereford looked startled, as if he'd just been stung by

9
00:00:47.257 --> 00:00:48.318
a wasp.

10
00:00:48.338 --> 00:00:50.980
"I know those men!"

11
00:00:51.281 --> 00:00:52.702
he shouted in surprise.

12
00:00:52.722 --> 00:00:59.808
"They're—" "Robert of Locksley and his friends," the queen said with a smile.

13
00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:04.062
Robin used this name when he was in disguise.

14
00:01:04.803 --> 00:01:08.906
The bishop's face was red with anger, but he didn't say anything more.

15
00:01:08.926 --> 00:01:12.288
"Locksley!" the queen called to Robin.

16
00:01:12.308 --> 00:01:14.510
"I've made a bet with the king.

17
00:01:15.291 --> 00:01:19.394
I told him that you and your men can outshoot any of his men.

18
00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:23.717
I hope, for my sake, that I'm not wrong."

19
00:01:23.737 --> 00:01:26.839
"We'll do our best for you!"

20
00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:27.840
said Robin.

21
00:01:28.584 --> 00:01:31.966
Little John shifted his feet, looking a little shy.

22
00:01:31.986 --> 00:01:35.949
"You're so lovely, Queen Eleanor," he said.

23
00:01:35.969 --> 00:01:39.271
"Is there anyone who wouldn't do their best for you?"

24
00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:42.033
The queen laughed.

25
00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:44.714
But the bishop didn't crack a smile.

26
00:01:45.655 --> 00:01:47.036
And neither did King Henry.

27
00:01:47.696 --> 00:01:49.217
He was glaring at his wife.

28
00:01:49.237 --> 00:01:52.379
"Who are these men?"

29
00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:53.640
the king demanded.

30
00:01:55.424 --> 00:01:58.866
Before the queen could speak, the bishop leaped to his feet.

31
00:01:58.886 --> 00:02:01.988
"Locksley is really the outlaw Robin Hood!"

32
00:02:02.368 --> 00:02:03.188
he burst out.

33
00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:09.132
"That giant fellow is called Little John, and the other one is Will Scarlet.

34
00:02:09.812 --> 00:02:11.833
They both belong to Robin Hood's band.

35
00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:15.255
All three of them are robbers and thieves."

36
00:02:16.956 --> 00:02:18.537
The king looked stunned.

37
00:02:18.557 --> 00:02:20.318
"Is this true?"

38
00:02:20.738 --> 00:02:22.219
he asked the queen sternly.

39
00:02:22.239 --> 00:02:26.661
"Yes," the queen replied, smiling.

40
00:02:27.262 --> 00:02:29.423
"The bishop knows these men well.

41
00:02:30.303 --> 00:02:35.046
He and some of his friars spent three days with them in Sherwood Forest.

42
00:02:35.847 --> 00:02:41.550
Remember, dear, you promised these archers would be safe for forty days."

43
00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:44.492
"I'll keep my promise."

44
00:02:44.812 --> 00:02:45.752
The king scowled.

45
00:02:45.772 --> 00:02:51.596
"But when those forty days are up, Robin Hood should beware.

46
00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:56.334
Things may not go exactly as he wants."

47
00:02:57.956 --> 00:03:00.498
He turned to Gilbert, Tepus, and Hubert.

48
00:03:00.518 --> 00:03:05.102
"If you beat Robin Hood and his men, I'll reward you well.

49
00:03:07.304 --> 00:03:09.545
Go now, and do your best."

50
00:03:12.528 --> 00:03:17.272
The men began to get ready, stringing their bows and carefully selecting their arrows.

51
00:03:17.872 --> 00:03:19.133
The match began.

52
00:03:19.354 --> 00:03:22.016
No one had ever seen such amazing shooting.

53
00:03:22.696 --> 00:03:25.959
Hubert went first, and made his best shots of the day.

54
00:03:26.559 --> 00:03:28.000
Will Scarlet went next.

55
00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.483
He shot too cautiously and couldn't beat Hubert.

56
00:03:34.064 --> 00:03:36.226
Little John easily beat Tepus.

57
00:03:37.327 --> 00:03:41.890
Gilbert tried his best and hit two bull's-eyes with his three arrows.

58
00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.572
"Well done, Gilbert!"

59
00:03:45.092 --> 00:03:46.774
Robin slapped him on the shoulder.

60
00:03:46.794 --> 00:03:49.816
"You really should come to Sherwood Forest."

61
00:03:50.548 --> 00:03:55.611
He picked up his bow, selected an arrow, and then instantly shot a bull's-eye.

62
00:03:56.271 --> 00:03:57.472
The crowd gasped.

63
00:03:57.492 --> 00:04:03.656
"There's nothing interesting to shoot here in London," Robin said to Gilbert.

64
00:04:04.516 --> 00:04:06.117
He shot another bull's-eye.

65
00:04:06.557 --> 00:04:08.718
"What do you think?"

66
00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:13.701
Robin hit another bull's-eye.

67
00:04:14.722 --> 00:04:18.284
A murmur went through the crowd and then everyone started clapping.

68
00:04:19.036 --> 00:04:21.098
Gilbert rushed to shake hands with Robin.

69
00:04:21.118 --> 00:04:24.762
"I think you're the best archer in the world!"

70
00:04:25.743 --> 00:04:27.544
King Henry wasn't so gracious.

71
00:04:27.564 --> 00:04:31.448
"It's time for us to go," he snapped at Queen Eleanor.

72
00:04:32.969 --> 00:04:37.954
They stood up and left the field, without watching the judges give Robin first prize.

73
00:04:38.815 --> 00:04:43.740
Robin won a trumpet, a purse of gold coins, and ten gold arrows.

74
00:04:53.596 --> 00:04:57.238
"I'll keep this silver trumpet," said Robin after the ceremony.

75
00:04:57.258 --> 00:05:00.519
"But, Gilbert, you shot the best of the king's men.

76
00:05:00.919 --> 00:05:04.200
So I am giving you the purse of gold coins."

77
00:05:04.741 --> 00:05:06.501
At this, the crowd cheered.

78
00:05:06.521 --> 00:05:10.023
"What will you do with the ten gold arrows?"

79
00:05:10.423 --> 00:05:11.323
asked Little John.

80
00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:15.405
"I'll give them to the top ten archers," replied Robin.

81
00:05:16.005 --> 00:05:18.586
Another loud cheer rose from the crowd.

82
00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:21.908
Robin handed out the arrows to the men.

83
00:05:22.624 --> 00:05:24.345
"Keep them to remember this day.

84
00:05:24.785 --> 00:05:26.905
It was an honor to compete against you."

85
00:05:26.925 --> 00:05:30.186
"Hooray!" cried the crowd.

86
00:05:30.206 --> 00:05:32.627
"Hooray for Robin!"

87
00:05:33.487 --> 00:05:37.228
The archers swarmed around Robin and his men, eager to meet them.

88
00:05:37.908 --> 00:05:39.609
Everyone was talking loudly.

89
00:05:40.769 --> 00:05:43.530
A member of the king's guard tapped Robin's shoulder.

90
00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:46.751
"I have a message for you," said the guard.

91
00:05:46.771 --> 00:05:50.352
"The queen's page said to tell you: The lion growls.

92
00:05:50.552 --> 00:05:52.961
Beware. Do you know what that means?"

93
00:05:53.841 --> 00:05:55.381
"Yes." Robin nodded.

94
00:05:55.401 --> 00:05:57.522
"Thank you for delivering this warning."

95
00:05:58.102 --> 00:05:59.083
He turned to his men.

96
00:05:59.103 --> 00:06:00.303
"Little John!

97
00:06:00.643 --> 00:06:02.444
Will! We must be going."

98
00:06:03.724 --> 00:06:07.366
As they hurried away, Robin explained the reason for their haste.

99
00:06:07.386 --> 00:06:10.087
"That was a message from the queen," he said.

100
00:06:10.107 --> 00:06:12.327
"King Henry is furious!"
